{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996547-need-help-with-my-adventure","id":996547,"title":"Need help with my adventure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T06:13:52-07:00","id":996547,"title":"Need help with my adventure","content":"Hi, new here. Whats up?<br /> Im playing M:TAw for a almost a year now. we are a group of 3 players and a storyteller. we meet once a moth for a 2 day weekend because we were having a hard time finding time to play every week or every second week. now, up until now i was playing, but the storyteller is tired of running the game and want to join as a player and I'm the only logical replacement.<br /> its been years since I've been in the GM seat, and I'm not sure how to write for MTAw... so far i have an idea, but i need help flashing out the antagonists and their mechanics. here is what i got so far, ill add questions i have in the end. <br /> oh, and we are playing guardians and its 1st addition, we haven't made the switch yet.<br /> ---this adventure contains sexual abuse of women and children and violence towards children, if you don't wish to be exposed to this kind of content, don't read any further--<br /> this adventure is inspired by the life of j.m Berrie, the author of Peter Pan and an alleged child molester.<br /> the adventure takes place in London. children has been disappearing from Kensington gardens and the area of the gardens for the past few months, and the police has no leads on the subject.<br /> the antagonist is the kidnapper. Hes name is Jaimie Allen, and he is an orderless acanthus. he was raised by a single alcoholic working class mother in a country plagued by the neo-liberalism of Margaret thatcher. never knew his father, the closest thing he had for a father image is his mother abusive boyfriend, also a working class man, but of better means because he does not support a child nor is he a single woman. both Jaime and his mother were abused by this man, both sexually and physically, for his somewhat effeminate nature. he grew up an introvert, writing and painting magnificent worlds. his awakening took place on the year of his 23rd birthday. he has crippling social anxiety and a great love for children, because of a childhood taken away from him. until something happened.<br /> questions:<br /> i kinda want to use the abyss as a turning point in the life of Jaime, somehow turning Jaimie into a hikikomori type of guy, a deranged lunatic who kidnaps children and try to stop them from growing, or maybe he thinks he is waking them up or something. they die when he fails, but its unclear whether by accident or by design. i don't know how this stuff works. if you have suggestions about what made him this way, or what magical purpose might kidnapped children have, i will be glad to hear it.<br /> i also want it to have a sense of mystery and horror. they are trying to find out who or what is making the children disappear, but i don't have a hook to make them start investigating. what makes the guardians interested in the disappearances of sleeper children?<br /> i want it to have a sense of urgency, maybe they need to get to the bottom of it before someone else does? thinking about adding a seers pylon or something. but i don't know what motives might a seers pylon have.<br /> also, I will be very thankful if some of you might have ideas for how can an investigation story like this naturally progress (at the start they only know that children are disappearing), and how does a good investigation scene in mage look like.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if my post is hard to understand, English is not my first nor second language.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12613-audacity","name":"audacity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:25:42-07:00","id":996550,"title":"","content":"Clear the text formatting ( it's hard to read ) , mark 1st Edition in context, write some sum-up on Players Characters - then we could help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:48:11-07:00","id":996557,"title":"","content":"If they catch a whiff of the Abyss that ought to be enough.<br /> <br /> Maybe something is left behind in the corpses, a sprinkling of black dust that caused their brains to flood with endorphins until their brains fried, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:07:56-07:00","id":996564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996547-need-help-with-my-adventure?p=996550#post996550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clear the text formatting ( it's hard to read ) , mark 1st Edition in context, write some sum-up on Players Characters - then we could help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>except for the sum ups, i have no idea how to do what you just asked. i didn't use any special text formating (at least not on purpose), and don't know how to add tags of whatever.<br /> the sum ups: there will be a new character joining, right now unknown to me. the other two are somewhat similar.<br /> the first is an thyrsus, 2 gnosis, he is mostly about stealth and combat. has a 1 dot in death, 2 in life and 3 in spirit. his most important tool when it comes to investigating is calling spirits and interrogating them.<br /> the other one is an moros with a few dots in space. her tool is scrying, obviously, and calling ghost agents. she is also into electronics and computers.<br /> i hope the third one will be a social character to fill that hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12613-audacity","name":"audacity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:22:21-07:00","id":996571,"title":"","content":"Expanding on my original suggestion: Abyssal pixies use their dust to cause children to enter a shared state of hallucinations. The children in this state have their happiness harvested in order to keep powering the pixies magic. The author of Pan stumbled across this phenomenon when the children living next door were harvested. He finances himself by writing stories from the ravings of the children in the throes of the dust. You can decide if his profits are purely mundane or if he's managed to coerce or cooperate with the pixies for further nefarious ends.<br /> <br /> You have two routes for investigation, the corpses of the children with suspicious shared symptoms of death, or the Temenotic realm of Nevernever that's begun to intrude into the local consciousness as more children succumb to their fevered dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:08:23-07:00","id":996592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996547-need-help-with-my-adventure?p=996571#post996571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding on my original suggestion: Abyssal pixies use their dust to cause children to enter a shared state of hallucinations. The children in this state have their happiness harvested in order to keep powering the pixies magic. The author of Pan stumbled across this phenomenon when the children living next door were harvested. He finances himself by writing stories from the ravings of the children in the throes of the dust. You can decide if his profits are purely mundane or if he's managed to coerce or cooperate with the pixies for further nefarious ends.<br /> <br /> You have two routes for investigation, the corpses of the children with suspicious shared symptoms of death, or the Temenotic realm of Nevernever that's begun to intrude into the local consciousness as more children succumb to their fevered dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks, love that. i think he thinks he is using the pixies to help children, but actually they are using him. maybe he joins the children in astral space.<br /> have any thoughts about other antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12613-audacity","name":"audacity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:20:36-07:00","id":996603,"title":"","content":"Well, you could ask yourself if where the pirates figure in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:27:24-07:00","id":996607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>audacity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996547-need-help-with-my-adventure?p=996592#post996592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks, love that. i think he thinks he is using the pixies to help children, but actually they are using him. maybe he joins the children in astral space.<br /> have any thoughts about other antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>When the children enter a shared state of hallucation they connect with the Abyss. Are these children sort of aberration or are they cursed? You could play around with both ideas, if you want, but both lead pretty naturally to a story involving Scelesti. Whatever the answer abyssal entities attach to the children. From now on whenever the children go to sleep the entities come out to feast.<br /> <br /> The Adamantine Arrow is first drawn to the increased Scelesti activity in the area. They have lost the children to this kidnapper, who doesn't know what he has in his hands. Now it is a race between the Selestic and the Adamantine Arrow cabal. Who will get to the children first? And if the player characters reach them first, then what then? Kill them? There's every possibility that they are innocent children, even if they are tainted by the Abyss. Drive away the abyssal entities? More will probably come now that the children have been attuned to the Abyss. Take them to the Mysterium for study? Well, is that really any better than killing them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:48:20-07:00","id":996823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996547-need-help-with-my-adventure?p=996603#post996603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you could ask yourself if where the pirates figure in.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCaptain Hook could be a goetic demon left by the original Pan author, or maybe he is an Acamoth; the spirit of Freedom through Tyranny.<br /> \u200bAs far as bringing Guardian attention to the case, all you need is Sleepers who witnessed magic during one of the kidnappings. Yes they will forget and rewrite their memories but the initial confused reports would bring Guardian investigators in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 11-01-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:33:02-07:00","id":997059,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of great ideas here already, so the only real thing I can add is this: get your Chronicle's Theme and Mood down tight. So long as you keep the story and characters tied to either one or both, the story will be consistent on a basic level.<br /> <br /> Going off the ideas that are floating around I'll just spitball some examples.<br /> <br /> Theme: Innocence lost is gone forever.<br /> <br /> Mood: Bleak Reality, Breathtaking Fantasy<br /> <br /> ~ The Antagonist: Abused as a child and robbed of innocence at an early age, Jaimie Allen sought to use his Awakened magic to protect the children of London from the cruel reality of the Fallen World. However, he has become tarnished himself and cannot do good for these children no matter how hard he tries. He must regain his innocence, and the faeries have shown him the way. He has journeyed deep into the Neverlands and shed his humanity to become one of the Neverones. The innocent will be spared from the horrors of reality, and live forever with him as inhuman creatures.<br /> <br /> ~ The Seers: This era in history will either see the formation of the Ministry of Hegemony or be it's hight of power. The servants of the Unity use British nationalism and classism to chain the Sleepers of Britain into roles they will be forced to play for their entire lives, and both the Sleeping and Awakened few who see through this Lie are powerless to change the status quo. While the Diamond works within both high and low society to set into motion change that will shake the Seer's power base, society remain a quagmire of inequality and injustice. All one can do is simply exist within the Lie, and try to preserver until London is ready to shake off the yoke of Hegemony.<br /> <br /> That's all I've got for now. Hope it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}